# Survey – generated by the "question-me" skill

Background in plain terms: today, if the worker (runner) loses contact with the main server for a moment in the middle of a task — a short network blip or a server restart — the worker stops itself and restarts. This task would let it ride through those short outages instead.

## Round 1

```survey-json
{
  "round": 1,
  "generatedAt": "2026-11-23T08:11:38.000Z",
  "stage": "question-me",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "When the connection to the main server drops briefly in the middle of a task (a short network blip or a server restart), what should the worker do?",
      "options": [
        "Stay alive, report what happened, and keep checking for work (Recommended)",
        "Stop and restart itself, like it does today",
        "Mark the task as failed and move on to the next one"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "Which problems should the worker survive (stay alive) and which should still stop it?",
      "options": [
        "Only survive short connection problems (network errors, server busy or restarting); still stop for login problems, outdated orders, and anything unknown (Recommended)",
        "Survive short connection problems AND unknown errors too; stop only for login problems and outdated orders",
        "Survive everything and never stop on its own"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "When the worker is idle — just asking 'any new work?' or sending its regular 'I'm alive' signal — and the server briefly doesn't answer, what should it do?",
      "options": [
        "Retry a few times with growing waits, then keep waiting without restarting (Recommended)",
        "Just wait a few seconds and check again (simplest, no retries)",
        "Restart itself, like it does today"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q4",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "What should you see in the logs when the worker rides through a short outage?",
      "options": [
        "A clear one-line note naming the cause, then it keeps going (Recommended)",
        "Nothing special — just keep going quietly",
        "A loud warning every time it happens"
      ],
      "required": false,
      "showIf": null
    }
  ],
  "answers": {
    "q1": {
      "selected": [
        "Stay alive, report what happened, and keep checking for work (Recommended)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q2": {
      "selected": [
        "Only survive short connection problems (network errors, server busy or restarting); still stop for login problems, outdated orders, and anything unknown (Recommended)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q3": {
      "selected": [
        "Retry a few times with growing waits, then keep waiting without restarting (Recommended)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q4": {
      "selected": [
        "A clear one-line note naming the cause, then it keeps going (Recommended)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    }
  }
}
