6| *   or const/let/var binding, plus `export default`) must carry an `@example`
7| *   tag in its nearest preceding JSDoc block. Exports that were already
8| *   missing `@example` when the gate landed are recorded in
9| *   `scripts/baselines/jsdoc-example-missing.json` and keep passing untouched
10| *   (q6: the current gap stays a to-do); only exports NOT in that baseline —
11| *   i.e. newly created or newly renamed exports — fail. Runs across api/,
12| *   shared/, and frontend/src/ (q2/q8) and is wired into `npm run docs:check`.
13| * @example node scripts/check-jsdoc-example.mjs (exit 0 on a clean tree)
14| * @example node scripts/check-jsdoc-example.mjs --baseline-write
15| * @example node scripts/check-jsdoc-example.mjs --report
16| * @example node scripts/check-jsdoc-example.mjs --strict
